File System Access through the embedder's file chooser, on every system.

Android's WebView has WebContentsDelegate::UseFileChooserForFileSystemAccess:
showOpenFilePicker(), showSaveFilePicker() and showDirectoryPicker() go to
the delegate's RunFileChooser(), as <input type=file> does, instead of
content's own FileSystemChooser straight to the system's dialog. zebkit
decides file choosers in the application's hook (zebkit_view_on_file_chooser),
and File System Access opened the system's picker around it: the delegate
method, its listener adaptor and the branch that uses it are no longer
Android's only (the file types as UTF-16 from a FilePath, wide on
Windows). A delegate that returns false (the default) changes nothing.
docs/SYSTEM_INTEGRATION.md, section 9.

